HOW TO READ THIS
==============================================================================
  Pick the smallest margin for which, in EVERY context:
    - conv = True (the whole complex, not just its 1-skeleton, has
      stopped changing as the probe count grows), and
    - the shape has not collapsed relative to margin 0 -- a margin
      that buys stability by finding nothing is not a good margin.
  Then read the same table across corrections and alphas: a margin
  that only stabilises under one correction has not been calibrated,
  it has been fitted.
  The dose-grid table is a correctness check, not a choice: membership
  is settled at full dose and every grid contains full dose, so inv must
  be True everywhere -- a False there is a bug to chase, not a result.
  mono says the filtration only moved later as the grid coarsened, which
  is what landing on the first available grid point does, and shift is
  the resolution cost, which should sit at the 1/K scale. Those two can
  fail honestly, but only where the dose-response table shows ragged
  trajectories: check there before treating a False as a bug.
  The monotonicity table counts admitted simplices whose test fires,
  stops, and fires again. Those are the ones for which 'minimum
  effective dose' is a stretch: the filtration marks where the
  flickering stopped, and gap is how much of the dose axis lies between
  that and the first crossing. If this is near zero the dose-response is
  effectively monotone and the fixed-sequence reading is clean; if it is
  not, that is an argument for a trend test on the trajectory rather
  than for a different correction.
  The null/n column counts admitted 1-simplices whose |theta|/sigma AT
  FULL DOSE sits inside the null region |theta|/sigma <= margin -- false
  discoveries by the study's own point estimate. Full dose, not peak,
  because that is where membership is decided. It is a plug-in
  diagnostic rather than an unbiased FDR estimate, but every correction
  is scored against the same estimates, so it compares them fairly.
  It is undefined at margin 0, where the null region is empty -- which
  is exactly why a point null makes the comparison vacuous.

